### Why this is the optimal placement:
 1. **Transaction Safety:** Because this method is annotated with @Transactional, if the database fails while copying the rows to the new batch, everything rolls back seamlessly. No orphaned data will be left behind.
 2. **Smooth Handoff:** Once we finish the database shift and update dto.setBatchId(splitBatchId), the existing locking mechanism takes over automatically. self.executeAsyncBatchProcessing is called with the DTO pointing to the new batch, meaning the background worker and the Oracle Stored Procedure will execute perfectly without needing any modifications to their logic.
To guarantee that the UPDATE JOURNAL_REQUEST ... WHERE JOURNAL_ID LIKE ? query executes instantly, please ensure your DBA has created an index on (BATCH_ID, JOURNAL_ID) on the JOURNAL_REQUEST table.
